  "bugsFoundAndFixedThisPass": [
    "cloth on the WHOLE mesh put his face in the solver -- his jaw softened visibly while every number passed. Now a hair-only sim object; the skin cannot deform by construction.",
    "Blender cloth simulates in OBJECT-LOCAL space and ignores object-level animation, so an animated o.matrix_world produced a head that turned and hair that never felt it. The turn is driven by the head BONE now.",
    "in background Blender the point cache never builds from frame stepping alone -- it must be baked explicitly, and an unbaked cache reads as exactly 0.00 mm of motion.",
    "writing armature-deformed positions into the render mesh while it still carried its own Armature modifier applied the rotation TWICE; Kabsch cancelled it and the secondary motion read exactly 0.000 mm on every frame.",
    "the 'pinned region is rigid' gate was measuring HAIR ROOTS, which are inside the cloth and are supposed to give. It now measures the SKIN, which is what it was named for.",
    "lag by comparing two argmaxes over a full oscillation reported 17 frames on a signal whose true cross-correlation lag was 0 -- it had picked opposite half-cycles.",
    "'secondary motion' that subtracted only the roots' TRANSLATION reported 29.4 mm of phantom motion at r=0.97 lag 0 -- a rigid yaw sweep, since a tip far from the pivot travels a long way with no deformation. Kabsch removes the full rigid transform."
  ]
